    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Obtain a routine EEG and brain MRI, then capture typical spells on ambulatory EEG with video; start antiseizure medicine only if the spells prove epileptic. Guideline: Evidence-based guideline: Management of an unprovoked first seizure in adults (Krumholz A, et al. Neurology 2015;84(16):1705-1713) (2015) [S]</item><item>Overnight polysomnography followed by a multiple sleep latency test to evaluate excessive daytime sleepiness. Guideline: Treatment of central disorders of hypersomnolence: an American Academy of Sleep Medicine clinical practice guideline (Maski K, et al. J Clin Sleep Med 2021;17(9):1881-1893) (2021) [S]</item><item>Start modafinil 100 mg each morning with two scheduled 15-minute naps a day; check blood pressure and heart rate at follow-up. Guideline: Treatment of central disorders of hypersomnolence: an American Academy of Sleep Medicine clinical practice guideline (Maski K, et al. J Clin Sleep Med 2021;17(9):1881-1893) (2021) [S]</item><item>Stop daily ibuprofen, limit acute treatment to 2 days a week, and keep a headache diary. Guideline: The International Classification of Headache Disorders, 3rd edition (Cephalalgia 2018;38(1):1-211) (2018); The American Headache Society Consensus Statement: Update on integrating new migraine treatments into clinical practice (Ailani J, et al. Headache 2021;61(7):1021-1039) (2021) [S]</item><item>Start non-sedating headache prevention with candesartan, titrated after a potassium and creatinine check. Guideline: The American Headache Society Consensus Statement: Update on integrating new migraine treatments into clinical practice (Ailani J, et al. Headache 2021;61(7):1021-1039) (2021) [S]</item><item>Screen mood, anxiety, trauma symptoms, and cognition at baseline with a trauma-informed approach, and repeat the PHQ-9 at follow-up. Guideline: Evidence-based guideline: Management of an unprovoked first seizure in adults (Krumholz A, et al. Neurology 2015;84(16):1705-1713) (2015); Treatment of central disorders of hypersomnolence: an American Academy of Sleep Medicine clinical practice guideline (Maski K, et al. J Clin Sleep Med 2021;17(9):1881-1893) (2021) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
